Moreover, Kurtz does not teach or suggest the features of claim 16. Claim 16 includes the features that "the temporal segments of the noise signal (SNoise) are gathered by the anesthetizing monitoring unit within an adjacent time interval (TNoise) notoverlapping with a stimuli signal interval (Tstimu SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.160.25 and the duration of the responsesignal (TResponse)." This feature is representatively depicted in FIGS. 2A and 2B of the current application, reproduced above. In contrast, as noted above, the method of Kurtz involves dividing the noisy signal into a set of individual responses to the plurality of stimuli. Thus, the noise signal in Kurtz is gathered during the stimuli signal interval.
